---
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";
---

<section
  id="about"
  data-section-name="About"
  tabindex="-1"
  aria-label="About Manvendra Rajpoot"
  class="section-reveal mb-28 max-w-180 text-center leading-8 outline-none sm:mb-40 scroll-mt-28"
>
  <SectionHeading>About me</SectionHeading>

  <div
    class="rounded-2xl border border-black/5 bg-white px-6 py-8 shadow-sm sm:px-10 sm:py-10 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-white/5"
  >
    <p class="mb-3">
      I'm a <span class="font-medium">backend developer</span> who enjoys building
      systems that are scalable, secure, and quietly reliable. Across my roles at{
        " "
      }
      <span class="font-medium">CloudTechTiq</span> and <span
        class="font-medium">Radixlink</span
      >, I've designed and shipped multi-tenant SaaS platforms, central
      authentication systems with multi-factor auth and role-based access,
      payment integrations across Stripe, Razorpay and PayPal, and AI-powered
      features — from automated invoice extraction to grammar correction in
      customer support. My core stack is Python, Django, DRF and FastAPI, backed
      by PostgreSQL, Redis and MongoDB, and shipped with Docker, Kubernetes and
      CI/CD. <span class="italic">My favorite part of the job</span> is the problem-solving
      — turning a messy, manual process into a clean, automated system that just works.
    </p>

    <p>
      I care most about the things users never notice: API security, real-time
      notifications, background-job systems, and disaster-recovery plans that
      keep data safe and services running. On the frontend I work with React,
      Next.js and TypeScript, so I can take a feature from the database all the
      way to the browser. I'm currently pursuing my Master of Computer
      Applications at Jain University after completing my BCA at Bundelkhand
      University, and I never stop <span
        class="decoration-purple-500 underline decoration-2 underline-offset-2 dark:decoration-purple-400"
        >learning</span
      > — a new framework, a cloud service, or a better way to architect a backend.
      I'm open to <a
        href="#contact"
        class="text-purple-700 decoration-2 underline-offset-2 font-medium underline transition hover:text-pink-600 dark:text-purple-300 dark:hover:text-pink-400"
        >backend and full-stack roles</a
      > where I can build things that scale.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
